1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,000
This is a fully virtual warehouse rover project.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:13,825
It combines linear and nonlinear control, a friction-sensitive robot model, real ROS two messaging, and an editable controller PCB.

3
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:17,275
This demonstration uses recorded measurements.

4
00:00:17,275 --> 00:00:19,750
No physical hardware is required.

5
00:00:20,950 --> 00:00:27,644
The real-world problem is loss of traction when a loaded warehouse rover crosses a slippery patch.

6
00:00:27,644 --> 00:00:31,606
Independent wheel and body dynamics model that difference.

7
00:00:31,606 --> 00:00:35,978
A delayed pose sensor, encoders, and an IMU feed the controller.

8
00:00:35,978 --> 00:00:43,150
Physics runs at one kilohertz, wheel control at two hundred hertz, and trajectory control at fifty hertz.

9
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:50,462
The linear controller uses an L Q R trajectory loop and inner wheel P I control with anti-windup.

10
00:00:50,462 --> 00:00:54,558
This is a replay of the recorded sixteen second curved-route run.

11
00:00:54,558 --> 00:00:58,528
The rover follows the reference through the traction challenge.

12
00:00:58,528 --> 00:01:07,350
The moving-reference design is controllable and stable, and the worst dry-floor lateral error in the matrix is under nine millimeters R M S.

13
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:13,323
The nonlinear controller uses heading-dependent sine and cosine terms.

14
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:19,186
Its supervisor estimates slip from wheel speed and independent ground-speed estimates.

15
00:01:19,186 --> 00:01:24,709
Persistent slip reduces acceleration and torque, then hysteresis allows recovery.

16
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:28,391
Here, both runs use the same reference and noise seed.

17
00:01:28,391 --> 00:01:34,050
The supervisor is active only when the sensor-based traction estimate calls for it.

18
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:43,473
The comparison contains four controllers, three traction conditions, three payloads, three routes, and five noise seeds.

19
00:01:43,473 --> 00:01:46,351
All five hundred and forty runs completed.

20
00:01:46,351 --> 00:01:56,424
Supervision reduced low-traction integrated slip by eighteen point eight percent with L Q R and eighteen point five percent with nonlinear control.

21
00:01:56,424 --> 00:01:59,850
The planned twenty percent hypothesis was not met.

22
00:02:01,050 --> 00:02:08,132
The ROS test executed real publishers, subscribers, transforms, and a controller-selection service.

23
00:02:08,132 --> 00:02:15,071
It recorded and replayed a ROS bag, receiving four hundred and thirty replayed odometry messages.

24
00:02:15,071 --> 00:02:20,651
This diagram explains the tested graph; it is not a live ROS screen recording.

25
00:02:20,651 --> 00:02:26,517
The corrected Gazebo model also received real wheel torque through the ROS bridge.

26
00:02:26,517 --> 00:02:34,600
Both dry and low-friction cases moved the body, with increased wheel and body divergence on the slippery surface.

27
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:41,703
These are actual three-dimensional renders from the installed KiCad ten application.

28
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:51,682
The custom, two-layer Pico carrier connects external motor drivers, encoders, an IMU, current filters, and a latched drive authorization gate.

29
00:02:51,682 --> 00:02:55,266
It has twenty-nine components and twenty-nine nets.

30
00:02:55,266 --> 00:03:04,191
The repaired schematic and board have zero electrical rule violations, zero layout rule violations, and zero unconnected items.

31
00:03:04,191 --> 00:03:08,970
Library keepouts, copper clearance, and drill spacing are respected.

32
00:03:08,970 --> 00:03:14,100
The editable project and exports are included on the desktop and website.

33
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:24,761
Ngspice measured the current-sense filter time constant as one point zero zero one milliseconds, close to the one millisecond design value.

34
00:03:24,761 --> 00:03:29,322
The external driver signal is centered at one point six five volts.

35
00:03:29,322 --> 00:03:39,600
The virtual board includes signed twelve-bit current sensing, PWM quantization, command delay, an independent overcurrent trip, and a latched watchdog.

36
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:49,133
Five fault cases disable the drive: overcurrent, command timeout, encoder dropout, stale localization, and IMU bias.

37
00:03:49,133 --> 00:03:51,504
The faults start at five seconds.

38
00:03:51,504 --> 00:03:57,753
Qualification and timeout delays range from zero to one hundred and forty milliseconds.

39
00:03:57,753 --> 00:04:07,451
Cutting drive power does not stop motion instantly: the modeled rover coasts between one point one zero and one point four four meters.

40
00:04:07,451 --> 00:04:09,750
It has no emergency brake model.

41
00:04:10,950 --> 00:04:16,077
Four local wall-clock-paced tests each ran for approximately sixteen seconds.

42
00:04:16,077 --> 00:04:21,336
All met the twenty millisecond compute budget, with no compute deadline misses.

43
00:04:21,336 --> 00:04:26,929
The worst ninety-ninth percentile compute time was two point one three milliseconds.

44
00:04:26,929 --> 00:04:32,188
Compute duration and operating-system wake-up lateness are measured separately.

45
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:36,050
These are soft real-time results on a normal Windows host.

46
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:44,847
Requirements, linear control, nonlinear control, ROS integration, and software testing have executed evidence.

47
00:04:44,847 --> 00:04:51,409
The plant model passes its mathematical checks and its separate Gazebo torque and contact test.

48
00:04:51,409 --> 00:04:58,108
The editable PCB passes local KiCad rule checks and its current filter passes circuit simulation.

49
00:04:58,108 --> 00:05:05,982
The GitHub demo website includes interactive measured replays, comparisons, project downloads, and a profile link.

50
00:05:05,982 --> 00:05:09,850
GitHub verification tests remain manual at your request.

51
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:17,621
The video, phase report, and interactive demo website are delivered through your GitHub project.

52
00:05:17,621 --> 00:05:21,112
The editable KiCad project is also on your desktop.

53
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:28,847
The report includes the measured comparison, live timing, fault results, PCB findings, and reproducible commands.

54
00:05:28,847 --> 00:05:34,323
The project demonstrates control-engineering methods and industry design intent.

55
00:05:34,323 --> 00:05:41,100
It does not establish safety certification, manufacturing readiness, or physical robot performance.
